course: dictionary
lesson: 15188
title: Secrete: make it or hide it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Secrete is one of these words. In science, to secrete means to make a liquid or substance and give it out from a part of a body or a plant. «The stomach secretes acid to help break down food.» The stomach is making something, so secretes means makes and gives out.
explain: In a story, secrete can mean to hide something in a secret place. «Mia secreted the letter in her drawer so nobody would find it.» Nobody is making a letter here. Mia is hiding it, so secreted means hid.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is something being made, or is something being hidden? Then swap in make or hide and check that the sentence still makes sense. The noun is secretion, which is the liquid or substance that is given out.
fact: Secrete is a verb. Its other forms are secretes, secreted and secreting.
fact: Science meaning: «secrete» means to make and give out a liquid or substance from a part of a plant or animal body.
fact: Glands secrete sweat, tears and saliva. Bees secrete wax, and some frogs secrete poison from their skin.
fact: Story meaning: «secrete» can also mean to hide something secretly.
fact: The noun for this process is secretion.
exercise: «Bees secrete wax to build their honeycomb.» What does secrete mean here? | To sell something cheaply | *To make and give out a substance | To hide something secretly | To melt something in the sun
exercise: «Sam secreted the spare key under a flowerpot.» What does secreted mean here? | Made a new liquid | Lost it forever | *Hid it in a secret place | Showed it to everyone
exercise: Which word is the noun for the act of secreting? | secret | secrete | secretary | *secretion
test: «Our skin secretes sweat when we get hot.» Which word means the same as secretes here? | freezes | *produces | hides | breaks
test: «The thief secreted the gold coins inside his coat.» What does secreted mean? | Counted them loudly | Gave them away to children | *Hid them in a secret place | Melted them down
exam: Which sentence uses secrete to mean hide? | The stomach secretes acid to digest food | *The spy secreted the map under his bed | Bees secrete wax to make honeycomb | Glands secrete saliva in your mouth
